ise within their catalogue  of material is stargame  they always knew that amazon were  interested in this because amazon had  been showing the stargate cv series on  their platform on prime for the last few  years and have always done really good  sales and views  they knew amazon were interested but  as only a back catalog  it has a limited value stargate though  as an existing possible new tv show  holds more value so brad wright was  instructed to begin that process however  that all changed in march when steve  sparks lost his job  and the whole idea of a tv show and  animated series very much in line with  what amazon had done with star trek and  what i think mgm thought amazon would  want them to do has now been scrapped  michael wright mgm's new chief executive  of scripted tv  never liked this idea  he apparently believes that mgm don't  really have the production capabilities  to produce a high enough quality  animated series  he wants the new project to go in line  with what mgm already does and already  does well  but i'll tell you a bit more about that  in a minute  so where is this information coming from  right basically i did a video like i  said about a year ago that video did  really well i got 100 000 views it did  phenomenally well and i thank you all  for watching  and from that video i got a little  comment meant just happened to say this  actually isn't really true anymore  this was true about six months ago but  it's been scrapped i was intrigued by  that because he was so confident and  clear about what he was saying he was  you know he wasn't just sort of saying  like i don't think this is true he said  it's not true  so i started a little conversation with  him  now over the last month he has told me  lots of information and  he's basically unable to share that i  wanted him to come on and actually have  an interview and a conversation with him  but he said there's no chance he can do  that with his company he has actually  signed a non-di