 so i've got no reason to  disbelieve him but obviously he's making  some quite big claims and why would he  tell me at the end of the day  well he basically was only having a  conversation with me and he promised me  made me promise not to tell anyone but  last week he gave me permission he said  okay you can tell anyone just don't use  my name and don't tell me there's  certain things i'm not allowed to tell  you but anyway we'll move on from that  so brad wright has been quite openly  talking about how he's been developing a  new stargate series  my source says that that was very much  on purpose mgm very early on realized  amazon were very interested in the  stargate franchise but  as it was only a back catalogue its  value was limited  however stargate as a proposal move was  for a new tv show  and a tv show that people are actually  excited to hear about and to watch  held more value and could in theory get  more money for mgm  obviously james bond is by far their  biggest  franchise  and there's a lot of excitement around  james bond at the moment because daniel  craig is finished  they wanted something similar a hype  around stargate so brad wright started  talking quite openly about developing  this tv show he has spoken to amanda  tapping about potentially directing he  has spoken to michael shanks about  potentially directing and none of that  has been kept secret and the internet  has been abuzz with it  the giant freaking robot story probably  was purposefully leaked because at the  time it was true and again they wanted  people talking about stargate because  they wanted to drive the amazon interest  in buying the franchise and maybe  getting a little bit more money out of  them  it worked  amazon look at social media movement  they look at numbers they show stargate  on prime at the moment and it still gets  really good numbers you can't actually  get sg1 on prime in the uk even though  the show's 20 years old you have to pay  for it and people still 